    <statement><p>Find the following integral.  Note that you can check your answer by
differentiation.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle  \int\,\frac{\ln^{7}\mathopen{}\left(z\right)}{z}\,dz =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.125\ln^{8}\mathopen{}\left(z\right)+C</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>w = \ln(z)</m>.  Then 
<m>dw = \frac{1}{z}\,dz</m>, so that
<me>\int\,\frac{\ln(z)^{7}}{z}\,dz = 
  \int\,w^{7}\,dw = {1\over 8}\,w^{8} + C =
  {1\over 8}\,(\ln(z))^{8} + C.</me>



</solution>
